{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I was at the pharmacy this morning when I started having chest pain. It’s sharp and dull, comes and goes, and sometimes goes down my left arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Is it worse with activity or breathing? And have you had this before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s not worse with movement. It’s been happening on and off for a while, actually—similar to past visits. But today it came with nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea—five loose stools by midday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any blood in the stool? Or fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No blood, no fever. But I did fall a few days ago and hit my head and left side. And I’ve been having blurry vision off and on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for letting me know. We did an EKG and checked your heart enzymes. No signs of a heart attack. Your EKG shows some old changes but nothing new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart? But it feels so similar to before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of coronary disease with small vessels, we always take chest pain seriously. But your enzymes are normal twice now, and the EKG hasn’t changed. The pain also seems reproducible when I press on your chest wall, which suggests it could be musculoskeletal—like costochondritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. What about the diarrhea and stomach pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show no infection or inflammation. No white blood cell rise, liver tests are normal. Since you’ve had belly pain with eating before, and your CT scan recently was clear, we think this was likely a temporary GI issue. You haven’t had more diarrhea since arriving, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the blurry vision? That’s been bothering me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We reviewed your CT head from earlier today. No bleeding or stroke. The findings are chronic—likely from small vessel disease. But since you’re having visual symptoms, we recommend you see an ophthalmologist soon, within the next few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do that. What about my diabetes? My blood sugar was high this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-03-18 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was 247 this morning, but it’s manageable. You’re staying on your usual insulin—Lantus at bedtime and Humalog with meals. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve done well overnight—no more chest pain or GI issues. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. What should I do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking all your usual medications, including aspirin, Plavix, and your blood pressure and cholesterol pills. We’re adding Tylenol every six hours for the chest wall pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—please see your primary doctor soon. They may recommend a stress test. Also, schedule your GI appointment for the colonoscopy and EGD you’re due for, and don’t forget the eye doctor for your vision."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What if the chest pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If it’s severe, or if you have shortness of breath, nausea, or dizziness, go to the ER. Otherwise, call your PCP. But remember—your tests were reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better knowing it’s not my heart this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-03-19 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-03-19 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. Any pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-03-19 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just a little sore when I move, but the Tylenol helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-03-19 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, and keep up with those appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-03-19 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I will."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-03-18 20:36:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-03-19 18:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old woman with a history of coronary artery disease, diabetes, hypertension, and hypercholesterolemia was admitted for non-exertional chest pain radiating to the left arm, accompanied by nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. Initial evaluation showed no ischemic changes on EKG and normal cardiac enzymes. Chest pain was reproducible on palpation, suggesting a musculoskeletal origin such as costochondritis. Abdominal symptoms resolved during the stay, with no signs of acute infection or inflammation. A CT head showed no acute findings, though chronic small vessel disease was noted. The patient remained stable, with chest pain resolving by discharge. She was discharged home with instructions to continue her cardiac and diabetes medications, take acetaminophen for pain, and follow up with her PCP, GI specialist, and ophthalmologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Diarrhea",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
